    // This is a strict check to prevent reading files from subdirectories or
    // any location outside the specified 'dir_path'.
    // For example, if base_path is /var/www and filename is ../etc/passwd,
    // canonical_file_path would be /etc/passwd, and its parent_path() would be /etc.
    // Since /etc != /var/www, the access is rejected.
    // This also correctly handles cases where filename is "." or "..", as their
    // parent_path() would not match canonical_base_path.
    if (canonical_file_path.parent_path() != canonical_base_path) {
        return ""; // Path traversal attempt detected or file is not a direct child.
    }

